  "body": "The spec references the term \"scheme data\", claiming it's from the URL spec, but that term no longer exists in URL.  I haven't done history-diving, but it looks like \"scheme data\" was the name for the stuff after the scheme in non-hierarchical URLs, like `blob:`, and now those are just folded into the hierarchical stuff.  (If I'm reading correctly, a `blob:` URL would now have a host and a single path component.)\n\nI haven't looked at where all \"scheme data\" is actually used in HTML, but wherever it is needs to be updated to no longer use that term.\n",
